<title>POLAND: VISTULA, TRADE UNIONS AGREE ON JOB CUTS.</title>
<headline>VISTULA, TRADE UNIONS AGREE ON JOB CUTS.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish garment maker Vistula SA and trade unions have agreed on group lay-offs in its plant in Przeworsk, southern Poland, the company said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>Vistula did not give any other details.</p>
<p>Last month Vistula said it planned to lay off 206 of its 500 Przeworsk employees as the factory was moving to a one-shift system. -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
